From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:18:01 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 03/45] inkling2: family skeleton for the CUDA engine

Config parse that refuses shapes the kernels do not cover, the chat wiring
(marker ids from tokenizer_config.json, the stop id, the template check),
the reply split into reasoning, text and tool calls as vLLM's Inkling
parser reads it, admission to GB10 at two ranks (TF_INKLING2_RANK and
TF_INKLING2_WORLD through the environment table), and the attention
kernels' launch plan. Host tests run in test-cuda-host; the kernel image
builds with the rest. No weights are loaded yet.
